{"title":"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Bonus_Question\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Bonus Question</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_to_Bonus_Question\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution to Bonus Question</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an equilateral triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed096cb12bb4627f07259bd946a58ff827aefa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D,E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> on the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada6f54288b7a2cdd299eba0055f8c8d19916b4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/0936990e6625d65357ca51006c08c9fe3e04ba0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> respectively.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85a74cad6df8d737330bbcc412acc0a477c5a78d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF,EG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> (with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab647d696e2f613d32d866e816e3aeb7c94dc90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F \\in AE, G \\in AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" />) are the interior angle bisectors of the angles of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, prove that the sum of the areas of the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/7/65772dfa055c928d9b85ea6be539a35c1dff1b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEG$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is at most equal with the area of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.  When does the equality hold?\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44dd4d53c715d7722f7efd789c4c560fa8543084.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[DEF]}{[DEA]} = \\frac{EF}{EA} = \\frac{DE}{DE+AD}\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"43\" /> Similarly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962abf42782448e4553a4019200c800ea0512047.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[DEG]}{[DEA]} = \\frac{DG}{DA} = \\frac{DE}{DE+AE}\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"43\" /> Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c819a3f0194fef68d03566df2ceb112999796a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF] + [DEG] = DE[DEA](1/(DE+AD) + 1/(DE+AE))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"500\" height=\"18\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3dd088d0ab1e1de048a42d4faaba978ca3d53d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEA] = 1/2 AD\\cdot AE\\sin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea5a1d26aabcbac0b9135cd06cce97fd56aacd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC] = 1/2 AB\\cdot AC \\sin A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"215\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee301f7350e8859d09af7c7a2b64ff550a769f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{[DEF] + [DEG]}{[ABC]} = \\frac{DE\\cdot AD\\cdot AE}{AB^2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{(DE+AD) + 1/(DE+AE)}\\]\" width=\"512\" height=\"43\" />\nObviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192a2671ac4a674ba8a150e398725c3cd6dca40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE \\le AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />, so it is sufficient to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e0267d7d4c246ad28d79b9be3ab0b79de2542c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD\\cdot AE(1/(DE+AD) + 1/(DE+AE)) \\le DE (*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"409\" height=\"18\" />.\nThe cosine rule applied to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/41046dc59ecaddc8f7b03e89fc5a1f6bd874f4f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE^2 = AD^2 + AE^2 - AD\\cdot AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"248\" height=\"16\" />. Hence also  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abbb3af0e7c859a7ef86b83c5611f90bb37369cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE^2 - AD\\cdot AE = (AD - AE)^2\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"291\" height=\"21\" />. Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63ef56c25faf1358b8ee206182d245c68932053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE(AD - AE)^2 + DE^2(AD + AE) \\ge AD\\cdot AE(AD + AE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"471\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/d/30ddfc7526032685449e7ef6656bf4c33cd4f355.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD\\cdot AE(AD + AE + 2DE) \\le DE(AD^2 + AE^2 + DE(AD + AE)) = DE(DE + AD)(DE + AE)\\]\" width=\"711\" height=\"19\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d02e715e7f7195675151570530c5b62ba7b2744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(*)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Bonus_Question\">Bonus Question</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Bonus Question\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the above problem, prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b823de85f5167c923370978875dd81f634a347eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF/EG = AD/AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>- Proposed by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8a050ca0f84a6aef15ead346438c2777533f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Kris17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_to_Bonus_Question\">Solution to Bonus Question</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution to Bonus Question\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927d4689159fbeb80f7b468ca9ae96b48e926312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is an angle bisector of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/70422100db8de33f8e5e0ab5062c5bb6a5ac969d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADE$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />.\nExtend line DE to meet BC at H.\nLet us define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0beb78d266c72807247b07045151d9c46ff75517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DHB = \\theta$\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b06124b21d0dbc12447387d9e2a12c41ca9ea53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PDE = (60^{\\circ} - \\theta)/2 = (30^{\\circ} - \\theta/2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"18\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926b773b0cf84d272ff62419a6ede859a598763a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PED = (60^{\\circ} + \\theta)/2 = (30^{\\circ} + \\theta/2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"282\" height=\"18\" />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59fb18554160498701076495ac05d5af2519253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DPE = 180^{\\circ} - (\\angle PDE + \\angle PED) = 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"346\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/6160ed1b549214b3e5b75a371c5d31614c9ffe1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AGPF$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral.\nSo we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66f2b24881d7d5cbd0982b47e2cfebf2b7dd3a49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GFP = \\angle GAP = 30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"183\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e0a43bd3c66d0885810e319225f86378bb2bf77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PGF = \\angle FAP = 30^{\\circ}$\" width=\"183\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04debb4692ccd9c49438b83a85a25a1637d9bc00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GFP = \\angle PGF$\" width=\"135\" height=\"12\" />, implying that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/70632d625ec605cff7a576af81bd7023be1b1612.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PGF$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is an isoceles triangle.\nSo we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b36758908e2e4c919ee1e92976375a02c294840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PG = PF$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Also, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b5a13d542296146fad12c409bcd3761f8cc8f13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GPD = 180^{\\circ} - \\angle DPE = 60^{\\circ} = \\angle DAF$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"325\" height=\"13\" />,\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb30e30ea37ad4356c4203c1008aaf8073d7d8de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GDP = \\angle ADF$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />, it follows that:\ntrianlge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06652aa2a7b2d77f371004d07fb91f350e09728d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GDP$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> ~ triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651bffb059906f373d826a5030b415fdc31e3729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Similarly it can be shown that:\ntrianlge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2ed1737c767012db19524e067a543c3f7dbe0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FEP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> ~ triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fdedf5200397f35c61277c1da005058e24d647d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEG$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>From trianlge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06652aa2a7b2d77f371004d07fb91f350e09728d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GDP$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> ~ triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651bffb059906f373d826a5030b415fdc31e3729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de19787cf28d497a4f6d299c0e582701eb230a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PG/AF = DG/DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/3/e938711e61202715e490d2c62f3e379bc1f16627.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PG = AF(DG/DF)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>From triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2ed1737c767012db19524e067a543c3f7dbe0ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FEP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> ~ triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fdedf5200397f35c61277c1da005058e24d647d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEG$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ad4ec4c1feb5cbf412033d522e5d608c8560cb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PF/AG = FE/GE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3b82c0833b1100b628e6bec864b89bfcf227be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PF = AG(FE/GE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b36758908e2e4c919ee1e92976375a02c294840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PG = PF$\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81190b5b83eb2c41d8652e49ecd710cccb59fb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF(DG/DF) = AG(FE/GE)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"242\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45086718cfc6606fd436bdd565f38109bb663e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AF/FE)(DG/AG) = (DF/EG)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/13634804bd449b77efc2a30d4bd38f0cb94416bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AD/DE)(DE/AE) = (DF/EG)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b823de85f5167c923370978875dd81f634a347eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF/EG = AD/AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8a050ca0f84a6aef15ead346438c2777533f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Kris17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO\" title=\"2001 JBMO\">2001 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017034701\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 348/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 868/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 36/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10896/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.199      1 Template:JBMO_box\n100.00%   13.199      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16984:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017034701 and revision id 186113. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}